## Point CONTRIBUTING.md at a single contributor guide

Context: GitHub's repo-root CONTRIBUTING.md had drifted into a long copy of
setup, commit, and test instructions. Those belong in Help Center docs so
README, development, and code-organization can share one source.

Changes:

1. docs/contributing.md
   Added the canonical contributor workflow (setup, layout, style, tests,
   AI eval gate, changelog, Conventional Commits, PRs, Sphinx, releases).
2. CONTRIBUTING.md
   Reduced to a pointer plus a short local-run snippet.
3. README.md, docs/README.md, docs/development.md, docs/code_organization.md
   Linked the new guide.
4. .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
   Pointed authors at docs/contributing.md.

